<title>USA: Appliance Recycling gets contract.</title>
<headline>Appliance Recycling gets contract.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Appliance Recycling Centers of America Inc said Thursday that Edison International unit Southern California Edison Co signed a contract to extend and expand its refrigerator recycling program.</p>
<p>As previously disclosed, under terms of this agreement Edison has specified minimum refrigerator recycling volumes that will generate annual revenues of about $3.5 million per year in both 1996 and 1997.</p>
<p>Edison further agreed to take action that should significantly expand the program beyond the guaranteed minimum volumes.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
</text>
